      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1900-01-26_WidnesExaminer_art0008" n="art0008">
        <p>HOMOCEA. FOR THE BATTLE-HELD. NOTICE.</p>
        <p>uthT FAingorlhLealing , be provided with Homocea, as known. TROOPS F TIIE TRANSIt7hAerSeLis snhoothuilndg more HBOO3 FOR WOUNDS, Cuts, Bruises, Broken Skin, Sore Places, generally, use Homocea often, and plenty of it.</p>
        <p>INFAINTRY need Homocea for anointing the feet on the march, and for scpres caused by cbfing a2nutrements.</p>
        <p>C"ALRY need Homocea for troubleB cased by rough riding, damp saddles, etc., end especially for piles.</p>
        <p>SEE THAT NO FRIEND goes to the front without Homocea. What else can they rely on to touch the spot "and soothe the aching part " ?</p>
