        <p>NOTlCE.—Solvers who become entitled to a prize in this competition can, if they desire, have any book on the game of Draughts equal to the value of ss. instead of cash prize, by notifying the Draughts Editor. _</p>
        <p>In connection with the above competition we offer a monthly prize of ss. to the competitor who succeeds in placing himself at the head of the Solvers' List at the end of the month. Where the prize is awarded the winners' score is cancelled, while the remaining competitors' points go towards the next months competition. The winner may re- enter the tourney if he chooses, commencing again at the bottom of the list. Points are awarded as follows: Two for the correct solution of a prob- lem ; two for correcting the author's terms, one for showing a dual solution or a dual key-move, and one for showing a duel continuation at any stage in the solution.</p>
        <p>As will be noticed by the Solvers' List,several of our solvers have succeeded in pointing out a dual continuation to Problem No. 67. The dual continua- tion is, at sth move instead of 9-14, play 17-2 and B. wins. Several have also pointed out a dual solu- tion by playing instead of 14-9 at 3rd move. 17-21, 25-22. 21-25, 2-6, 25-30, 6-9, 14-17, 22 -13, 5-14, B wins We have accordingly awarded these solvers the extra points allowed.</p>
