        <p>Body Found in the Canal at Moore. The dead body of a man unknown was found floating in the Manchester Skip Canal at Moore on Friday afternoon. The following is the police des- cription of the deceased :—" Age, about 40 years ; rift. 10ins in height,stout build,with full round face; hair and moustache sandy, and turning grey left leg broken, clothed in a portion of a blue cotton shirt, brown cord trousers, pair of rod and white striped elastic braces, black leather belt round waist." The body had apparently been in the water about three weeks or a month. The deceased had the appearance of a labourer.—An inquest on the body was conducted by Mr. Dobson,at the Red Lion Inn, Moore, on Saturde.y afternoon, when a verdict of "Found drowned" wa4 returned.</p>
