        <p>WEEKLY REPORT ON THE HEALTH OF WARRINGTON. Week Ending Saturday, 13th, January, 1900. Durine the week the following births and deaths were registered : Births. Deaths. Warrington Registration District 54 26 The excess of births over deaths was 28. The Birth Rate was equal to 43•2 per 1,000. The death-rate from all causes was equal to 20 8 per 1,000, against 22.6 the average of the previous four weeks, and against 18.6 the corresponding period of last year. The death- rate from the seven chief zymotic diseases was equal to 0 8 per I,ooo,against 1•6 the average rate of the previous four weeks, and against 0.8 the corresponding period of 1899. The ages of mortality were- -0-1 1-5 5-15 15-25 25-65 65 up. Totals 2 3 2 1 10 8 26. The deaths included-1 from scarlet fever. 9 from lung diseases. 3 from heart diseases, 2 from injuries, 3 trom influenza, 8 frcm all other causes. The following cases of Infectious Disease have been reported during the week :—Scarlet fever 3 cases diphtheria, 1 case, enteric fever 2 cases, erysipelas, 1 case. Total number of patients in hospital week ending Sat- urday, 13:h January, 20. METEOROLOGY—The mean t(mperature was 38 Fah. and therefore 0.9 degrees higher than the preceding week. The maximum temperature 45 F., was recorded on the Bth inst., and the minimum temperature 29 F., on the 11th inst. The Rainfall measured .69 inch. The general direc- tiou was S. E. JOHN H. GORNALL, Medical Officer of Health.</p>
