        <p>OUR LOCAL CHURCHES. Wycliffe P.S.A. Society. There was an average attendance at the meeting of this society on Sunday afternoon when Mr. Pickavance presided over the proceedings. In a brief address based on the 13th and 14th vzrse3 of the first chapter of Hebrews, he spoke about" Ages" and showed how they took a dePp intuyst and ministered unto men.—ln the absence of the appointed speaker for tht! afternoon, the Rev. J. Yonge cieliver,d an addre,s and spoke upon the value of private prayer.—Miss Britch was the soloist and effectively' sang two act.los. The mvice was also taken part in by Mr. D. Owen.</p>
